WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.940
What if every patient taking a drug still gets worse?

2
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.340
Could it still be working?

3
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:10.440
Illness changes on its own, and knowing who got treated sways ratings.

4
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.960
Clinical trials and epidemiology build fair comparisons instead.

5
00:00:19.083 --> 00:00:22.863
To test a treatment fairly, split one group of people by chance.

6
00:00:24.183 --> 00:00:28.023
That chance split is a randomized trial, so both groups start alike.

7
00:00:29.323 --> 00:00:33.523
One group gets the treatment; the other gets a look-alike without the drug, a

8
00:00:33.523 --> 00:00:39.263
placebo. Neither patient nor rater knows which is which, keeping the trial

9
00:00:39.263 --> 00:00:40.263
double-blind.

10
00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:43.813
Take a large trial in early Alzheimer disease.

11
00:00:45.233 --> 00:00:50.613
People received lecanemab, an antibody that clears amyloid plaques, deposits between

12
00:00:50.613 --> 00:00:53.253
neurons, or a placebo for 18 months.

13
00:00:54.933 --> 00:00:56.593
Suppose treated patients still got worse.

14
00:00:57.873 --> 00:01:00.453
What must the placebo group show if the drug helped?

15
00:01:06.017 --> 00:01:08.337
The placebo group must decline faster.

16
00:01:09.717 --> 00:01:13.377
Both groups got worse, yet treated patients got worse more slowly.

17
00:01:14.717 --> 00:01:19.297
The gap between treated and placebo shows the effect: decline slowed without

18
00:01:19.297 --> 00:01:24.717
stopping. Random assignment and blinding separate a treatment's effect from bias,

19
00:01:25.237 --> 00:01:27.297
chance, and the disease's own course.

20
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.660
Even a biological change can mislead without clinical outcomes.

21
00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.520
An autopsy deposit shows what builds up, not whether it kills.

22
00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:43.820
Trials judge clinical outcomes like thinking, daily function, or survival, and

23
00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:51.480
measure harms. In fragile X syndrome, mavoglurant in 2016 and basimglurant in 2018

24
00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.420
were tested against placebo.

25
00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:57.780
Neither beat placebo on the main behavioural measures.

26
00:01:58.883 --> 00:02:02.443
You cannot randomly assign a harmful drug or infection.

27
00:02:03.783 --> 00:02:08.763
Instead, epidemiology tracks groups of people, called cohorts, across time and

28
00:02:08.763 --> 00:02:14.983
place. A small cohort without an independent control shows feasibility, not

29
00:02:14.983 --> 00:02:16.123
population efficacy.

30
00:02:17.683 --> 00:02:23.883
Defects after isotretinoin exposure in 1985 fit animal results, yet the human

31
00:02:23.883 --> 00:02:25.443
mechanism stayed inferred.

32
00:02:26.617 --> 00:02:29.117
Fair trials unlocked lasting prevention.

33
00:02:30.377 --> 00:02:34.637
A neural tube defect means the brain or spinal cord was left open.

34
00:02:35.937 --> 00:02:42.457
In 1991, the Medical Research Council Vitamin Study randomized women with a prior

35
00:02:42.457 --> 00:02:43.597
affected pregnancy.

36
00:02:44.977 --> 00:02:50.757
4 milligrams of folic acid daily, started before conception, cut recurrence by about

37
00:02:50.757 --> 00:02:56.297
72 percent. That is about seven of every ten recurrences prevented.

38
00:02:57.383 --> 00:03:03.983
In 1990, Delgado and colleagues studied 21 patients whose depression had remitted on

39
00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:09.763
antidepressants. Each patient received both a control and a challenge lowering

40
00:03:09.763 --> 00:03:14.183
tryptophan, serotonin's precursor, in double-blind crossover.

41
00:03:16.023 --> 00:03:20.903
Fourteen of the 21 relapsed after tryptophan depletion, while the control challenge

42
00:03:20.903 --> 00:03:22.543
had no significant effect.

43
00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:26.327
Epidemiology then pairs with biology.

44
00:03:27.667 --> 00:03:35.067
In 2015 and 2016, microcephaly tracked Zika, matching a 2013 to 2014 French

45
00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:36.147
Polynesia outbreak.

46
00:03:37.507 --> 00:03:43.047
In 2016, Mlakar and colleagues found Zika virus particles in a fetal brain.

47
00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:50.107
Ming, Song, and Tang showed Zika kills some cultured human cortical progenitors and

48
00:03:50.107 --> 00:03:56.087
slows the rest. Fair trials test treatments; cohorts and biology together trace

49
00:03:56.087 --> 00:03:56.587
causes.
